{"event_type":"review","id":"ebe58bf4fc2190ae0e27e7e86a187569e82fd4154f514069ebc2c8110b820d8d","occurred_at":"2026-11-07T05:17:03Z","payload":{"artifacts":[{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/5f29ead730818b40b5f094ca2adf050a18b97fa17777ee45a73929904ebd34be","sha256":"5f29ead730818b40b5f094ca2adf050a18b97fa17777ee45a73929904ebd34be"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/9ca9832c2469493f42f1c2a2a3babcf80d517d502048418abc5536409571e9d0","sha256":"9ca9832c2469493f42f1c2a2a3babcf80d517d502048418abc5536409571e9d0"},{"kind":"git-bundle","location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/5768b6c72fe74c63d99227b035b6d6cb6f1d74e49e497b35cda65b6c56d505bf","sha256":"5768b6c72fe74c63d99227b035b6d6cb6f1d74e49e497b35cda65b6c56d505bf"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/113b99738b6793066b4d22186f34dc89c8ae564443ec958a2b80e85c5d31c699","sha256":"113b99738b6793066b4d22186f34dc89c8ae564443ec958a2b80e85c5d31c699"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/f2690fc0c1946c2e012427528aeed7f0315da703b50fc4f498e24721c51c94ad","sha256":"f2690fc0c1946c2e012427528aeed7f0315da703b50fc4f498e24721c51c94ad"}],"attempt_id":"0238ac9843d1256b1bb087d6baf9ab2cfa0d18af83a01400c82597802680775b:0:1","base":"244cd33ee0164250c2a502dfc0fbf87879210bab","completion":{"errors":[],"exit_code":0,"scope_verified":true,"skipped":false,"terminal":true},"findings":[{"anchor_status":"unverified","blob":"3d4bec469d6f713bf8539b8d0adbf14a8669244b","body":"**One unscannable prior attempt burns the whole rescue round without calling the model.**\n\n- `failedAttemptFeedback` (Line 1140-1163) throws in four cases, all through `failedAttemptContents` (Line 1185-1206) or the patch cap:\n  - the prior failed commit touches a binary file;\n  - a file is over 4 MiB, including the parent copy of a deleted file;\n  - a file contains `\\uFFFD`;\n  - the patch is over 32 MiB.\n- Line 403 runs inside the attempt `try`. A throw lands in the catch at Line 925. That catch records an empty failed attempt (gate `none`), and the rescue round ends without invoking the model.\n- `rescueUsed` was already incremented and the escalation reservation was already taken. With `rescuePerPackageCap=1`, the package loses its only rescue.\n- Fix: treat the prior-attempt feedback as optional. If it cannot be built, send the rescue prompt without the patch and keep the reason. Do not fail the round.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Proposed fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n         if (decision.tier === 'rescue' && priorRound?.failedAttempt !== undefined) {\n-          priorFailedFeedback = await failedAttemptFeedback(git, priorRound.failedAttempt);\n+          try {\n+            priorFailedFeedback = await failedAttemptFeedback(git, priorRound.failedAttempt);\n+          } catch {\n+            // Feedback is advisory: an unscannable prior attempt must not\n+            // consume the rescue reservation without invoking the model.\n+            priorFailedFeedback = undefined;\n+          }\n         }\n```\n</details>","id":"7b204e7867f7bd9db22983d90c8e509113b6e0afe175d7d9e46eedf29ff4b00c","intervals":[],"path":"src/ops/sweep/taskLoop.ts","severity":"minor","source_id":null,"status":"untriaged","title":"One unscannable prior attempt burns the whole rescue round without calling the model."},{"anchor_status":"unverified","blob":"88e86612a8f6400a7cd820ba0fe27a9e6193b291","body":"**An injected `deps.observationWriter` refuses every event because the composition uses its own IDs.**\n\n- `compositionRunId` comes from `randomUUID()` (Line 347). `correlation.workId` comes from a fresh `randomUUID()` in `captureProvenance` (Line 253).\n- `ObservationWriter.append` rejects an event when `event.runId !== compositionRunId`. It also rejects a header whose `correlation.workId` differs from the writer's `workId` (`src/kernel/observation.ts:139-290`).\n- So with an adopted writer, the header append at Line 809 throws. Every later append is refused too: the `kernel-run-linked` event, `attempt-finished` events (the unit bindings get `observationRunId = compositionRunId`, Line 827), and `measurement-summary`. `observation.status` always ends as `indeterminate`.\n- The `ObservationWriter.workId` doc says an adopting composition \"takes BOTH identities from it (never a second, divergent allocation)\". This seam breaks that contract.\n- Only the test seam is affected; production opens its own writer. Fix: when `deps.observationWriter` is present, take `compositionRunId` and `workId` from it. Pass that `workId` into the correlation record instead of allocating a new one.","id":"0f2373801064de3e8747c589471cca3bfca0661073231768b2334bf321ab2539","intervals":[],"path":"src/ops/fix/runFix.ts","severity":"minor","source_id":null,"status":"untriaged","title":"An injected `deps.observationWriter` refuses every event because the composition uses its own IDs."}],"head":"a3dd8fe92b36f3f25138cdcb8595324c2b5db1db","head_tree":"a619b07177492e5c80d4ce45880731ec409f8b2c","input_scope":[{"blob":"8c3bb8d03d4f10fae6162ec578557a5dd9ee4162","intervals":[[53,77],[103,106]],"path":"docs/ops/fix.run.md"},{"blob":"18ce66fe85f247acfff5c7c292469a2d864b54ff","intervals":[[3,3],[5,5],[7,7],[12,12],[15,15],[19,19],[21,21],[27,28],[35,90],[104,104],[111,111],[118,118],[121,121],[128,128],[130,130],[136,137],[144,226],[240,240],[247,247],[254,254],[261,261],[268,268],[271,271],[278,278],[280,280],[286,287],[294,350],[362,362],[369,369],[372,372],[379,379],[381,381],[387,388],[395,431],[445,445],[452,452],[455,455],[462,462],[464,464],[470,471],[478,579],[593,593],[600,600],[607,607],[614,614],[621,621],[628,628],[631,631]],"path":"docs/transcripts/fix-run-escalation.md"},{"blob":"41778e72dd5d500f6408304cb7e41b8454b28453","intervals":[[5,23],[36,36],[42,43]],"path":"src/ops/fix/registry.ts"},{"blob":"88e86612a8f6400a7cd820ba0fe27a9e6193b291","intervals":[[9,30],[50,50],[55,55],[62,73],[83,98],[102,109